          "SparseSGD.Scaling.actual_curvature_noise_ratio_tendsto",
          "SparseSGD.Scaling.actual_dimension_correction_tendsto_one"
        ],
        "correction": "Exact ratios are p*B/(d+2-p) and (1-beta)*p*B/((1+beta)*(d+2-p)); the limiting constants use realizedBatchScale (the positive real scale for sigma>0 and the realized integer batch for sigma=0)."
      },
      {
        "id": "memoryless_edge",
        "status": "complete_corrected",
        "declarations": [
          "SparseSGD.Scaling.actual_sparse_memory_threshold",
          "SparseSGD.Scaling.scaled_dense_memory_ratio_tendsto_atTop",
          "SparseSGD.Scaling.scaled_critical_memory_ratio_tendsto_atTop",
          "SparseSGD.Scaling.scaled_fixed_memory_ratio_tendsto_atTop",
          "SparseSGD.Scaling.scaledRetention_gamma_zero"
        ],
        "correction": "The memoryless sign threshold is asserted on the sparse side kappa>sigma; the bookkeeping cuts introduce no extra phase boundary, though they can intersect resonance or switch boundaries. The gamma=0 edge has fixed retention, and sigma=0 uses the realized fixed integer batch."
